# Analysis report loglik decimals

When generating **temporary / analysis-only** reports (under `analysis_*/`, chat tables, STATUS drafts that are not finalized official records):

- Round and display **log-likelihood / selection-score** values to **two decimal places** (e.g. `−0.51`, not `−0.5114`).
- Apply the same to means, deltas, and Avg columns in markdown tables meant for quick reading.

Do **not** silently round away precision in underlying CSVs or scripts that feed official numerical audits unless the user asks; keep higher precision in machine-readable artifacts, display two decimals in narrative/temp tables.
